  "kanji": "編",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 編\ntitle: knit; compile\njlpt: 2\ntags: [jlpt-n2, grade-5, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 15\nradical: 糸\nradicalNumber: 120\nonyomi: [ヘン]\nkunyomi: [あ.む, -あ.み]\ndistractors: [紙, 約, 絡]\n---\n\n# 編 — knit; compile\n\n**Strokes:** 15 · **Key (radical):** 糸 (no. 120) · **JLPT:** N2 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n編 concerns knitting or braiding and also compiling or editing written material. Learn the complete word: 編集 concerns editing, while 編む can concern either textile work or compiling a book.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic, not etymology:** See 糸 beside the 扁-shaped right half and imagine threads being arranged like the material in a compiled book. This is an invented modern-shape association, not a historical or phonetic explanation.\n\nThe canonical key 糸, no. 120, appears in its compressed left-side form ⺯.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ヘン | on | [編集](../words/編集.md) へんしゅう - editing; compilation; [短編](../words/短編.md) たんぺん - short story; short film (ヘン becomes ぺん in this word) |\n| あ.む | kun | [編む](../words/編む.md) あむ - knit; braid; compile |\n| -あ.み | kun | 手編み てあみ - hand knitting |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [編む](../words/編む.md) あむ - knit; braid; compile\n- [編物](../words/編物.md) あみもの - knitting; knitted work, also written 編み物\n- [編集](../words/編集.md) へんしゅう - editing; compilation\n- [短編](../words/短編.md) たんぺん - short story; short film\n- 手編み てあみ - hand knitting\n\n## Notes\n\n- 編む is a transitive godan verb ending in む: 編みます あみます and 編んで あんで. The object takes を, whether it is something knitted or a book being compiled.\n- The leading hyphen in -あ.み marks a bound use, illustrated by 手編み てあみ. It is not a hyphen to insert in the Japanese spelling. The separate noun 編 へん can concern compilation or a volume.\n- [組む](../words/組む.md) くむ also has a dictionary braiding sense, besides assembling and teaming up. It is not an unrestricted opposite of 編む. Compare the shapes of [紙](紙.md), [約](約.md) and [絡](絡.md) without assigning them all the same meaning.\n\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project), 2026-10-21 snapshot. Word pairs: [JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1328360, 1397590, 1511870, 1511950, 1586670, 1597300, 1603240.\n",
